#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:14
msgid "Abstract"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:16
msgid "This PEP codifies an implementation of :pep:`752` for PyPI [1]_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:19
msgid "Motivation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:21
msgid ""
"Many projects and communities would benefit from the ability to reserve "
"namespaces. Since PyPI exists to serve the Python community, it is critical "
"to gather feedback to ensure that everyone's needs are met."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:25
msgid ""
"A dedicated PEP is required because the operational and policy nuances are "
"up to each package repository to decide."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:29
msgid "Rationale"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:31
msgid ""
"PyPI has been understaffed, receiving the first `dedicated specialist`__ in "
"July 2024. Due to lack of resources, user support has been lacking for "
"`package name claims <https://discuss.python.org/t/27436/19>`__, "
"`organization requests <https://discuss.python.org/t/33764/15>`__, `storage "
"limit increases <https://discuss.python.org/t/54035>`__, and even `account "
"recovery <https://discuss.python.org/t/43422/122>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:40
msgid ""
"The `default policy <approval-criteria_>`_ of giving paid organizations more "
"leniency when reserving namespaces provides the following benefits:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:43
msgid ""
"PyPI would have a constant source of funding for support specialists, "
"infrastructure maintenance, bug fixes and new features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:45
msgid ""
"Although each application would require independent review, less human "
"feedback would be required because the process to approve a paid "
"organization already bestows a certain amount of trust."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:50
msgid "Terminology"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:52
msgid "Paid/Corporate Organization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:53
msgid ""
"`Corporate organizations`__ are :pep:`organizations <752#organizations>` "
"that pay for special functionality on PyPI. This PEP refers to them as paid "
"in most circumstances for brevity and to ease understanding for non-native "
"speakers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:57 ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:135
msgid "Root Grant"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:58
msgid "A grant as defined by :pep:`PEP 752 terminology <752#terminology>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:59 ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:143
msgid "Child Grant"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:60
msgid ""
"A grant created from a root grant with the associated namespace being a "
"child namespace as defined by :pep:`PEP 752 terminology <752#terminology>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:66
msgid "Implementation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:69
msgid "Grant Applications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:72
msgid "Submission"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:74
msgid ""
"Only organization (non-user) accounts have access to the grant application "
"form."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:77
msgid ""
"Applications for paid organizations receive priority in the reviewing queue. "
"This is both to offer a meaningful benefit to paid organizations and to "
"ensure that funding is available for PyPI's operational costs, including "
"more reviewers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:85
msgid "Approval Criteria"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:87
msgid "The namespace must not be something common like ``tool`` or ``apps``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:88
msgid "The namespace should be greater than three characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:89
msgid ""
"The namespace should properly and clearly identify the reservation owner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:90
msgid "The organization should be actively using the namespace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:91
msgid ""
"There should be evidence that *not* reserving the namespace may cause "
"ambiguity, confusion, or other harm to the community."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:94
msgid ""
"Organizations that are not paid organizations will represent one of the "
"following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:97
msgid "Large, popular open-source projects with many packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:98
msgid "Universities that actively publish packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:99
msgid "Government organizations that actively publish packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:100
msgid ""
"NPOs/NGOs that actively publish packages like `Our World in Data <https://"
"github.com/owid>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:103
msgid ""
"Generally speaking, reviewers should be more tolerant of paid organizations "
"that apply for grants for which they are not yet using."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:106
msgid ""
"For example, while it's reasonable to grant a namespace to a startup or an "
"existing company with a new product line, it's not as reasonable to grant a "
"namespace to a community project that doesn't have many users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:111
msgid "Rejections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:113
msgid ""
"Rejected applications will receive clear rationale for the decision based on "
"the approval criteria. Applications rejected due to the namespace being too "
"common will be persisted internally for future reviewers to reference and "
"new applications attempting to reserve a namespace that was previously "
"rejected for that reason will display a warning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:120
msgid "Acceptance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:122
msgid ""
"When an application is accepted for a namespace that is used by projects "
"outside of the organization, an email will be sent to the owners of the "
"projects notifying them of the new grant. The email will contain a link to "
"the `namespace's page <namespace-page_>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:128
msgid "Grant Types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:130
msgid "There are two types of grants."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:137
msgid ""
"An organization gets a root grant for every approved application. This grant "
"may produce any number of `child grants <child-grant_>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:145
msgid ""
"A child grant may be created by the owner of a `root grant <root-grant_>`_ "
"at any time without approval. The namespace associated with such grants must "
"be a child namespace of the root grant's namespace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:149
msgid "Child grants cannot have their own child grants."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:154
msgid "Grant Ownership"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:156
msgid ""
"The owner of a grant may allow any number of other organizations to use the "
"grant. The grants behave as if they were owned by the organization. The "
"owner may revoke this permission at any time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:160
msgid ""
"The owner may transfer ownership to another organization at any time without "
"approval from PyPI admins. If the organization is a paid organization, the "
"target for transfer must also be a paid organization. Settings for permitted "
"organizations are transferred as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:168
msgid "User Interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:173
msgid "Namespace Page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:175
msgid ""
"The namespace of every active grant will have its own page that has "
"information such as its :pep:`open <752#open-namespaces>` status, the "
"current owners, the time at which ownership was granted and the total number "
"of projects that match the namespace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:181
msgid "Project Page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:183
msgid ""
"Every project's page (`example <https://pypi.org/project/google-cloud-"
"compute/1.19.2/>`__) that matches an active namespace grant will indicate "
"what the prefix is (NuGet currently does not do this) and will stand out as "
"a pill or label. This value will match the ``prefix`` key in the :pep:"
"`namespace detail API <752#namespace-detail>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:190
msgid ""
"Clicking on the namespace will take the user to `its page <namespace-"
"page_>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:194
msgid "Visual Indicators"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:196
msgid ""
"For projects that match an active namespace grant, users will be able to "
"quickly ascertain which of the following scenarios apply:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:199
msgid ""
"Projects that are tied to a `grant owner <grant-ownership_>`_ will not have "
"a visual indicator and users should solely rely on the always-present prefix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:202
msgid ""
"Projects that are not tied to a `grant owner <grant-ownership_>`_ and the "
"matching grant is :pep:`open <752#open-namespaces>` will have a unique "
"indicator that does not convey mistrust or danger. A good choice might be "
"the `users <https://fontawesome.com/icons/users>`_ icon from Font Awesome or "
"the `groups`__ icon from Google Fonts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:207
msgid ""
"Projects that are not tied to a `grant owner <grant-ownership_>`_ and the "
"matching grant is restricted will have a unique visual indicator. This "
"situation arises when the project existed before the grant was created. The "
"indicator will convey inauthenticity or lack of trust. A good choice might "
"be a warning sign (⚠)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:216
msgid "Open Namespaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:218
msgid ""
"When a `child grant <child-grant_>`_ is created, its :pep:`open <752#open-"
"namespaces>` status will be inherited from the `root grant <root-grant_>`_. "
"Owners of child grants may make them open at any time. If a grant is open, "
"it cannot be made restricted unless the owner of the grant is the owner of "
"every project that matches the namespace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:225
msgid "Grant Removal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:227
msgid ""
"If a grant is shared with other organizations, the owner organization must "
"initiate a transfer as a prerequisite for organization deletion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:230
msgid ""
"If a grant is not shared, the owner may unclaim the namespace in either of "
"the following circumstances:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:233
msgid "The organization manually removes themselves as the owner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:234
msgid "The organization is deleted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:236
msgid ""
"When a reserved namespace becomes unclaimed, the `UI <user-interface_>`_ "
"will reflect this such that matching projects will no longer have any "
"indicators on their page nor will the namespace have a dedicated page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:241
msgid "How to Teach This"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:243
msgid ""
"For organizations, we will document how to reserve namespaces, what the "
"benefits are and pricing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:246
msgid ""
"We will document :pep:`541` on the same pages so that organizations are "
"aware of the main mechanism to report improper uses of existing packages "
"matching their grants."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:251
msgid "Rejected Ideas"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:254
msgid "Page for Viewing All Active Grants"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:256
msgid ""
"There is no page to view all active namespace grants because this has the "
"potential to leak private information such as upcoming products."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:260
msgid "Visual Indicator for Owned Projects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:262
msgid ""
"There is no indicator for projects that are tied to a `grant owner <grant-"
"ownership_>`_ primarily to reduce clutter, especially since this is the most "
"common scenario."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0755.rst:266
msgid ""
"If there was an indicator, it would not be a check mark or similar as NuGet "
"chose because it may mistakingly convey that there are associated security "
"guarantees inherent to the use of the package. Additionally, some social "
"media platforms use a check mark for verified users which may cause "
"confusion."
msgstr ""

